# Build context is the repository root, so this file matters a great deal:
# without it, Docker uploads node_modules and every bin/obj directory to the
# daemon on every build. That is typically hundreds of megabytes and turns a
# two-second context transfer into a minute.

**/bin/
**/obj/
**/out/
**/publish/
**/.vs/
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/

# Node / frontend — never needed by a .NET image build
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.vite/
**/.angular/
**/.expo/
**/storybook-static/
**/playwright-report/
**/test-results/
web/
mobile/

# Docs, tests and infra are not inputs to a service image
docs/
tests/
deploy/
identity/
.github/
*.md
!README.md

# Local environment and secrets must never enter an image layer. Even a deleted
# file remains in the layer history and is trivially recoverable from the image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/*.pfx
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/secrets.json
**/appsettings.Local.json

.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
